     I don't remember the details, but I think it was that the
weight of a cursed bag of holding wasn't recalculated correctly
after contents were randomly destroyed upon opening.  So you
could fill one up with something you didn't mind losing--tons
of rocks were in vogue--access it repeatedly to destroy those,
then have a bag which had negative weight so allowed you to
carry lots of other stuff.  I'm pretty sure that was before
encumbrance was introduced, when you could either move normally
or be so overloaded that you couldn't move at all, with none
of the intermediate slowed movement stages.

